  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Market Development Facility Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Market Development Facility (MDF) Phase 2 aims to create additional employment and income opportunities for poor women and men through sustainable and broad-based pro-poor growth.  
MDF analyses market dynamics and socio-economics to identify industries and sectors that can provide benefits for the poor, as customers, consumers, owners or employees of targeted small enterprise.
MDF reduces the risks and costs of pre-commercial 
or early-stage opportunities, and supports innovation 
through a blend of financial 
and non-financial support including: co-investment to  help de-risk innovation and test 
new products, services and business models; market analysis to understand consumer and 
business trends; technical advice to develop new products/services and business models; and marketing and promotion. 
Phase 2 is implemented Fiji, Timor-Leste, Sri Lanka, PNG (until 2022), Samoa, Vanuatu and Tonga (since 2022) through Palladium in partnership with Swisscontact.</narrative>
  </description>
